  "notes": [
    "A2 5bfda3b is immutable: no source pixels, proportions, position, default character colours or game files changed. Native 96x96 cells, S SE E NE N NW W SW; foot [48,94].",
    "Material domains were located separately per direction; shared RGB values are not assigned one material across the sheet. Blue-grey trousers/stockings are cloth 6; cape outside and lining are house 8. Exposed fingertips and ears are skin 3.",
    "Brown eye brows are hair 4. Upper lashes, pupil, sclera and highlights are fixed eye 2. Only the iris is 5. Original smile retained; mouth G0 and cheek G1 are fixed 10. Rear NE/N/NW contain no eye or mouth IDs.",
    "Small pale hanging hip cloth/paper and its sewn brown hem are cloth 6; its fastening leather strap is 7; visible metal buckle and brooch are copper 9. No new material ID is introduced.",
    "ID11 denotes dark inter-material boundary fragments; interior hair locks and cape folds retain their material shadow. Components are evaluated with 8-connectivity and 4-neighbour material contacts.",
    "G is determined monotonically from the original CIELAB L* within each material; official palette values and order are unchanged. The mask does not select or change the initial character palette.",
    "Signal exception approved by owner: #F9DA99 at S(47,53),(46,54),(48,55),W(39,53) brooch and S(47,64),(46,66) buckle =6 pixels, all ID9. Existing Sun/Blonde/Amber ramp exceptions remain locked. NW hair #EAB15C is ID4; keep-original default option remains for later D-A3-1 review.",
    "Official e1d74b4 QA: all 17 hard checks PASS; 640 colour combinations / 5120 direction images, all leak counters 0. Source PNG and RGBA hashes unchanged; shade-order inversions 0%. ID11 1350 px / 139 eight-connected groups (36.2% of 3729); every group touches >=2 distinct materials 3..10 by four-neighbour contact.",
    "Soft flags reviewed: 407 four-connected islands of size 1-2. Counts by ID: 1=307, 3=9, 4=22, 6=10, 7=15, 8=30, 9=6, 10=5, 11=3. ID1: immutable diagonal/staircase plum outline; cannot relabel its 1882 exact pixels. ID4: isolated brow tips and dark hair-rim steps. ID3: exposed fingertips and ear/face-rim fragments. ID8: cape/collar contour and fold steps separated by fixed boundary pixels. IDs6/7: small sleeve, cloth edge, glove and boot fragments. ID9: discrete copper trim/highlights. ID10: original smile corners. ID11: four-connected fragments belong to valid eight-connected boundary groups; no failing groups. These are retained source details, not added artwork.",
    "Other soft QA information: ID2 outside padded eye zones =0; side-view mouth G0 is E=3 px, W=2 px, preserving the original smiles. Per-ID source colour inventory is complete in source_colors; shared colours are intentionally listed under multiple materials when their native positions differ.",
